adjudication.rationale:
The diff intentionally adds a hard feature gate at the start of both `UpdateCompatibilityMetadata.run()` and `UpdateCompatibilityCheck.run()`:
```java
if (!Profile.isFeatureEnabled(Profile.Feature.ROLLING_UPDATES)) {
  printFeatureDisabled();
  picocli.exit(CompatibilityResult.FEATURE_DISABLED);
  return;
}
```
This is reinforced by updated docs stating the commands/operator will fail unless `rolling-updates` is enabled, and by tests that now pass `--features=rolling-updates` to make the commands work. The finding’s claim that `save-metadata --features=rolling-updates` still exits 4 when the feature isn’t enabled in the “persistent build” is not something the diff demonstrates (it depends on runtime semantics of `Profile.isFeatureEnabled` / persistence that are not shown). The “breaking metadata save on old-version pods during rolling upgrades” scenario is also not verifiable from this diff alone.
